{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T4Buhw4QDai22uLpeQNfJX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully.\nagentId: <scrubbed-agent> (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: <scrubbed-agent> to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using. Work on non-overlapping tasks, or briefly tell the user what you launched and end your response.\noutput_file: <scrubbed-path>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>","timestamp":"<scrubbed-timestamp>","tool_use_result":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"<scrubbed-agent>","description":"Codebase analysis for storage layer Q1","prompt":"You are the codebase-analyst in a speckit-autopilot consensus round. Resolve the following clarify question from the perspective of established code patterns and conventions in the existing codebase.\n\n**Question (Q1):**\nShould we follow the existing `src/storage/` abstraction (which the constitution endorses), or introduce a new layer specifically for the new resource type?\n\n**Your task:**\n1. Examine `src/storage/` and adjacent directories to understand the existing storage abstraction — its interfaces, extension points, conventions, and how current resource types plug into it.\n2. Look for prior examples of resource types being added to `src/storage/` versus introducing parallel layers. Note any patterns, base classes, factories, or registries that signal the intended extension model.\n3. Check whether the abstraction was designed to accommodate new resource types polymorphically, or whether it's tightly coupled to existing types in a way that would force a new layer.\n4. Identify any code-level evidence (file paths, line numbers, interface definitions, existing implementations) that supports your recommendation.\n\n**Output format:**\nReturn a structured answer with:\n- **Recommendation:** (extend `src/storage/` OR introduce new layer)\n- **Confidence:** (high / medium / low)\n- **Codebase evidence:** bullet list of file paths + line references and what each shows\n- **Caveats:** anything the orchestrator should know about edge cases or risks\n\nDo not synthesize across other analysts. Do not write files. Return your answer as the agent result.","outputFile":"<scrubbed-path>","canReadOutputFile":true}}
