{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NhTEZEMmAFJhSv1yWmhvAR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Spec/constitution analysis for storage layer Q1","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:spec-context-analyst","prompt":"You are the spec-context-analyst in a speckit-autopilot consensus round. Resolve the following clarify question from the perspective of the project constitution, technical roadmap, and prior spec artifacts.\n\n**Question (Q1):**\nShould we follow the existing `src/storage/` abstraction (which the constitution endorses), or introduce a new layer specifically for the new resource type?\n\n**Your task:**\n1. Read the project constitution (typically `memory/constitution.md` or `.specify/memory/constitution.md`) and locate the principle(s) that endorse the `src/storage/` abstraction. Quote the relevant language.\n2. Read the current feature's `spec.md` and `plan.md` (under the active feature directory in `specs/`) to understand what the new resource type is and how the spec frames its integration with storage.\n3. Check the technical roadmap and any prior completed specs for precedent — has a similar question been resolved before? What was the outcome?\n4. Identify whether the constitution's endorsement is a hard principle (NON-NEGOTIABLE / MUST) or a soft preference (SHOULD), and whether the spec articulates any reason this resource type would be an exception.\n\n**Output format:**\nReturn a structured answer with:\n- **Recommendation:** (extend `src/storage/` OR introduce new layer)\n- **Confidence:** (high / medium / low)\n- **Spec/constitution evidence:** bullet list of artifact paths + quoted language with section references\n- **Caveats:** any tension between constitution principles and the spec's framing, or open questions the orchestrator should weigh\n\nDo not synthesize across other analysts. Do not write files. Return your answer as the agent result."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
